eceived\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d18\"},\"ref\":\"d18\",\"snippet\":\" ... The winner of the 2010 Asian American Short Story Award, Yapa's fiction and nonfiction have appeared in American Short Fiction; Guernica; Hyphen; Literary Hub; The Margins; O, The Oprah Magazine; Poets & Writers; Slice; and others. He lives in New York City and teaches online and in the ... \",\"title\":\"https://pen.org/meet-the-2021-literary-awards-judges/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"a1a7a7a314d3367fc421df4b96ee53df04fa51d43c9d6556732950814ecb4452\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"c0dfe1fc3e6dd12f12bddbdb0ea8f25856fc47155a3ff74dc4a825ee554f7a2e\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Asian Literary Prize winners 2010s\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d28\"},\"ref\":\"d28\",\"snippet\":\" ... She was shortlisted for the 2016 Scotiabank Giller Prize for The Party Wall, which is an English translation of her French-language short story collection Le mur mitoyen. Leroux won the 2019 Governor General's Literary Award for English to French translation for her translation of Do Not ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/the-top-20-canadian-books-of-2024-so-far-1.7252475\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d21\"},\"ref\":\"d21\",\"snippet\":\" ... Scotiabank Giller Prize short list nominee in 2005, winner of the city of Toronto Book Award in 2000 and the recipient of the CBC Canadian Literary Award for short fiction in 2001. Her books have been published in 18 countries and translated into 14 languages and she was ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2007, Man Group plc established the Man Asian Literary Prize, an annual literary award given to the best novel by an Asian writer, either written in English or translated into English, and published in the previous calendar year.\\n\\nFor many years, as part of The Times Literature ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d29\"},\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... His award-winning novels have been adapted for the cinema, shortlisted for the Man Booker Prize, and translated into more than thirty languages. His essays and short stories have appeared in The New York Times, The Washington Post, and The New Yorker, among many other publications. Hamid now ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.aspeninstitute.org/blog-posts/20-new-works-fiction-social-impact/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d30\"},\"ref\":\"d30\",\"snippet\":\" ... prize more than once), Praiseworthy wins the UK's James Tait Black Prize and is shortlisted for the Dublin Literary Award and the Climate Fiction Prize, among others. Marosia Castaldi's The Hunger of Women wins the ALTA Prize for Prose (for the best translation from any language ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.andotherstories.org/about-us/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d31\"},\"ref\":\"d31\",\"snippet\":\" ... A selection of his poetry is collected in Desire Never … Read More\\n\\nColm Toíbín\\n\\nColm Toíbín is the author of six novels, including The Master, winner of the International IMPAC Dublin Literary Award and shortlisted for the Man Booker Prize, as well as winner of the LA Times ... \",\"title\":\"https://griffinpoetryprize.com/judges/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d32\"},\"ref\":\"d32\",\"snippet\":\" ... James English contends that prize culture is undergirded by a single-winner axiom, according to which each prize strives to be the prize that matters, the ultimate consecrator of literary value. We can see this logic at work in a letter from publisher Tom Maschler to Booker McConnell ... \",\"title\":\"https://giramondopublishing.com/heat/archive/beth-driscoll-how-prizes-work-in-the-literary-economy/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d18\"},\"ref\":\"d18\",\"snippet\":\" ... Lambda Literary Award-winning debut memoir, Man Alive (City Lights, 2014) was named one of the best books of the year by NPR Books, BuzzFeed, Kirkus, and Publisher's Weekly. His follow-up, Amateur (Scribner, 2018), was shortlisted for the U.K.'s Baillie-Gifford Book Prize for ... \",\"title\":\"https://pen.org/meet-the-2021-literary-awards-judges/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"f1919ecce6e9b74442ac15d1272a454db488afcf98d4f5b648066bd2d5d6ecd3\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"a3cdf97dc3fabb7b64a5c3ea88ec555feb1acfbe34e14c5d6d6db87b41af8aec\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Asian Literary Prize shortlist contender translated 25 languages\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_eviden