rary Association. Selvadurai's second novel Cinnamon Gardens was published in Canada, the U.K, the USA and was translated into 6 languages: Italian, French ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"6c8e7459aa5496fcb7d1b0a3ffb147036c27ac1c88377a329099185ca1447ad1\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"01eb51c27e202e88e3b9be3983f37769d651d5d60ef1ca69d914bfbb93830f92\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"novel translated into 25 languages award contender 2010s\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... Literary critics have noted that it is a mark of distinction for authors to be selected for inclusion in the shortlist or to be nominated for the \\\"longlist\\\".\\n\\nA sister prize, the International Booker Prize, is awarded for a work of fiction translated into English and published in ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d42\"},\"ref\":\"d42\",\"snippet\":\" ... His first two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were both finalists for the Booker prize. His novels have been translated into more than 29 languages and won the inaugural FT/Oppenheimer Award for Fiction, an NAACP Image Award, the LA Times Book prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d43\"},\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\" ... exuberant, coruscating translation.\\n\\n\\\"This is a luminous novel of India and Partition, but one whose spellbinding brio and fierce compassion weaves youth and age, male and female, family and nation into a kaleidoscopic whole.\\\"\\n\\nThe International Booker Prize 2022 Shortlist\\n\\n| Title | Author | Translator | Original Language | Author Residence | Publisher ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d44\"},\"ref\":\"d44\",\"snippet\":\" ... National Book Foundation\\n\\nThe National Book Award for Translated Literature, is one of five annual National Book Awards in the USA, recognising outstanding literary works of translation into English and administered by the National Book Foundation. This award was previously bestowed from 1967 to 1983 but did not ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Book_Award_for_Translated_Literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d30\"},\"ref\":\"d30\",\"snippet\":\" ... prize more than once), Praiseworthy wins the UK's James Tait Black Prize and is shortlisted for the Dublin Literary Award and the Climate Fiction Prize, among others. Marosia Castaldi's The Hunger of Women wins the ALTA Prize for Prose (for the best translation from any language ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.andotherstories.org/about-us/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d31\"},\"ref\":\"d31\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her books have been translated into more than fifty languages and have won dozens of international awards, including the Orange Prize, the Guardian Fiction Prize, the Lannan Award for Fiction, and the Commonwealth Poetry Prize for the Americas. Among many other honours, she is a Royal … Read More ... \",\"title\":\"https://griffinpoetryprize.com/judges/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d45\"},\"ref\":\"d45\",\"snippet\":\" ... Victorian Prize for Literature (worth $100,000) and the Fiction award (worth $25,000) at the 2023 Victorian Premier's Literary Awards.\\n\\nRead moreGiramondo Publishing, Fitzcarraldo Editions and New Directions are pleased to announce the shortlist for The Novel Prize, the biennial award for a book-length work ... \",\"title\":\"https://giramondopublishing.com/books/jessica-au-cold-enough-for-snow/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d46\"},\"ref\":\"d46\",\"snippet\":\" ... It has been translated into ten languages and enjoyed critical success all over the world. It is a winner of the Betty Trask award, a finalist for the MsLexia First Novel Prize, shortlisted for the Women's Prize for Fiction, the National Book Awards and the Sunday Times ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.deborahrogersfoundation.org/writers-award\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"8d7f9498fe75538e8f408b618c3269825cd78f59802f9fa47ecbd153b062d918\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"e556cb54cad12cefe616d2883843a11d63021359cf342743abdb226ecd0d4882\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"book translated into more than 25 languages literary prize shortlist\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_0f572733c3f745f08005f5f4"},{"content":"I found a strong lead: Chigozie Obioma's novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were both finalists for the Booker prize, and his novels have been translated into more than 29 languages. Let me investigate this further.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d42\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_2c8a8a94219a4d78a36700d7","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Chigozie Obioma born city birthplace\", \"Chigozie Obioma grew up hometown\", \"Chigozie Obioma biography birthplace Nigeria\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_b1f91ccbc23c46408e813b71","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d42\",\"document_chars\":17355,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"79767844ce2071fc5dcf3fb0e64d0cade0ba154ef0fc324d0054c1c767e63138\",\"snapshot\":\"90019ca46504785f620ef12f36abae20080c8c3bc7809053339e4beaa4deb2fd\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: ADVISORS\\ndate: 2022-01-01\\n---\\nADVISORS\\n\\nAdvisors\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was named one of Foreign Policy's 100 Leading Global Thinkers in 2015 and served as a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Distinguished Professor of English and Creative Writing at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Writers retreat. His third novel, The Road to the Country, was published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nRosie is a production and event manager based in Athens, Greece, with extensive experience in coordinating high-profile film festivals and cultural events. She holds a degree in Communication, Media and Culture from Athens and pursued further studies in Art History in Paris, culminating in a Master's in Culture & Tourism from Université Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne. Her professional experience includes collaborations with cultural organizations and festivals worldwide, including UNESCO in New York, the Rolex Art Festival, Les Rencontres d'Arles Photo Festival among others. Since 2018, she has served as Festival Coordinator and Special Events Manager for the French Film Festival of Greece, and since 2022, she has been the Head of Production for the Athens International Children's Film Festival. Driven by a deep passion for cultural engagement and sustainable tourism, she continually seeks innovative ways to connect communities through the arts. In her free time, she enjoys playing music and gardening.\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationaler Literaturpreis, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Professor of Creative Writing and English at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Fiction Writers program. His third novel, The Road to the Country, will be published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nKaterina Papanikolopoulos joined Faliro House in 2022 as Manager of Special Projects – a position that evolved into her role acting as the 2024 Oxbelly Retreat, Fiction Writers Program Manager. Following her graduation from UCLA (Summa Cum Laude, Art History), Papanikolopoulos founded the non-profit Athens Design Forum (ADF), a platform that advocates for overlooked and generative design histories interwoven with global labor and migration pa\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_2c8a8a94219a4d78a36700d7"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d42\"},\"ref\":\"d42\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2022-01-01\\n---\\nADVISORS\\n\\nAdvisors\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d47\"},\"ref\":\"d47\",\"snippet\":\" ... Farrell\\n*Karen Joy Fowler\\n*Linda Grant\\n*Abdulrazak Gurnah\\n*Sarah Hall\\n*Mohsin Hamid\\n*Shirley Hazzard\\n*Philip Hensher\\n*Mary Lawson\\n*David Lodge\\n*Patrick McCabe\\n*Colum McCann\\n*Tom McCarthy\\n*Shena Mackay\\n*Chigozie Obioma\\n*Michael Ondaatje\\n*Joseph O'Neill\\n*Tim Parks\\n*Caryl Phillips\\n*Julian Rathbone\\n*Mordecai Richler\\n*Arundhati Roy\\n*Bernice Rubens\\n*Donal ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d48\"},\"ref\":\"d48\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chigozie Obioma\\ndate: 2000-01-01\\n---\\n-\\n\\n- MajorsMinorsCertificates\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Policies & ProceduresFYW Guidebook\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Digital Learning LabsPortfoliosEvaluationsMoran ePortfolio AwardsBarnett Essay AwardsDouble Dawgs\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Transfer FAQProspective Student Information\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Study AbroadInternships and Research Opportunities\\n\\n>>\\n\\n-\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Double DawgsTransfer Student InformationDual Degree Progra\",\"title\":\"https://www.english.uga.edu/directory/people/chigozie-obioma\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d49\"},\"ref\":\"d49\",\"snippet\":\" ... This book brilliantly explores the effects of slavery and colonialism on African families as the story unfolds between West Africa and the United States.\\n\\n- The Fishermen (2015) by Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria): In this heartbreaking tale, four brothers in a small Nigerian town have their lives turned upside down ... \",\"title\":\"https://enkoeducation.com/the-must-read-in-african-literature/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d50\"},\"ref\":\"d50\",\"snippet\":\" ... the likes of US-based Nigerian Booker Prize shortlistee Chigozie Obioma to take on the mantle of bootstrap race \\\"analysis\\\" in a more sophisticated manner. A few months before the 2016 Aké Festival Black Lives Matter panel, Obioma saw it fit to make his intervention into the debate ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2019/04/why-im-no-longer-talking-to-nigerians-about-race\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d51\"},\"ref\":\"d51\",\"snippet\":\" ... Purple Hibiscus (2003), Half of a Yellow Sun (2006), Americanah (2013)\\n* Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria): The Fishermen (2015), An Orchestra of Minorities (2019)\\n* José Eduardo Agualusa (Angola): Rainy Season, Creole, The Book of Chameleons, My Father's Wives\\n* Ama Ata Aidoo (Ghana): Our Sister Killjoy (1977), Changes: a