slavery and colonialism on African families as the story unfolds between West Africa and the United States.\\n\\n- The Fishermen (2015) by Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria): In this heartbreaking tale, four brothers in a small Nigerian town have their lives turned upside down ... \",\"title\":\"https://enkoeducation.com/the-must-read-in-african-literature/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d47\"},\"ref\":\"d47\",\"snippet\":\" ... Farrell\\n*Karen Joy Fowler\\n*Linda Grant\\n*Abdulrazak Gurnah\\n*Sarah Hall\\n*Mohsin Hamid\\n*Shirley Hazzard\\n*Philip Hensher\\n*Mary Lawson\\n*David Lodge\\n*Patrick McCabe\\n*Colum McCann\\n*Tom McCarthy\\n*Shena Mackay\\n*Chigozie Obioma\\n*Michael Ondaatje\\n*Joseph O'Neill\\n*Tim Parks\\n*Caryl Phillips\\n*Julian Rathbone\\n*Mordecai Richler\\n*Arundhati Roy\\n*Bernice Rubens\\n*Donal ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d50\"},\"ref\":\"d50\",\"snippet\":\" ... Du Bois, and Malcolm X\\\" who understood that \\\"the future of their race could not be advanced by endless protests or marches of \\\"equality\\\" or \\\"justice.\\\"\\n\\nAfter dismissing the necessity of protest in struggle, Obioma goes on to hold up his country of birth Nigeria as an example ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2019/04/why-im-no-longer-talking-to-nigerians-about-race\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d48\"},\"ref\":\"d48\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chigozie Obioma\\ndate: 2000-01-01\\n---\\n-\\n\\n- MajorsMinorsCertificates\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Policies & ProceduresFYW Guidebook\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Digital Learning LabsPortfoliosEvaluationsMoran ePortfolio AwardsBarnett Essay AwardsDouble Dawgs\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Transfer FAQProspective Student Information\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Study AbroadInternships and Research Opportunities\\n\\n>>\\n\\n-\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Double DawgsTransfer Student InformationDual Degree Progra\",\"title\":\"https://www.english.uga.edu/directory/people/chigozie-obioma\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d51\"},\"ref\":\"d51\",\"snippet\":\" ... Oromay (\\\"The End\\\")\\n* Chinua Achebe (Nigeria): Arrow of God (1964), No Longer At Ease (1960), Things Fall Apart (1958), A Man of the People (1966), Anthills of the Savannah (1987), \\n* Chimamanda Ngozi Adichie (Nigeria): Purple Hibiscus (2003), Half of a Yellow Sun (2006), Americanah (2013)\\n* Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d52\"},\"ref\":\"d52\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chigozie Obioma, in The Orchestra of Minorities does the same. You shall notice in my next novel, The Wanderers [to be published in April/May], that I delve into this a little deeper also, to depict the notion of the absurdity of the human condition, which though popularized ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2021/03/the-xhosa-literary-revival\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d54\"},\"ref\":\"d54\",\"snippet\":\" ... Guardian Books Nigeria Limited, 1988), pp. 60–67\\n* Ogwude, Sophia O., \\\"History and Ideology in Chimamanda Adichie's Fiction\\\", Tydskrif Vir Letterkunde, 48.1 (2011), 110–123. \\n* Okonjo, Kamene, \\\"The Dual-Sex Political System in Operation: Igbo Women and Community Politics in Midwestern Nigeria\\\", in Nancy Hafkin and ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Thing_Around_Your_Neck\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"6ab1475eb4ce084209b5e379c986894ada925bd47c3636d8e9b0152a9466b689\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"a232f4d0174ca6fa2bca13ece675a5a5e4c77116ed778b1c04387965d6e7b571\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Chigozie Obioma biography birthplace Nigeria\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_b1f91ccbc23c46408e813b71"},{"content":"I have a strong lead. Chigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria, and his novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were both shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages. The Booker Prize was established in 1969, not the 2000s, so this doesn't fit the \"award created in the 2000s\" criterion. Let me reconsider.\n\nThe Man Asian Literary Prize (established 2007) fits \"award created in the 2000s.\" Let me check if Obioma's books were contenders for that prize, and verify the connection more carefully.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Asian Literary Prize shortlist 2010 2011 2012 2013 2014 2015\", \"Man Asian Literary Prize winners list all years\", \"Man Asian Literary Prize 2010s winner shortlist\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_ab718d407d5849d8a2362273","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Asian Literary Prize Wikipedia\", \"Man Asian Literary Prize established 2007 winners\"], \"top_k\": 5}","name":"search"},"id":"call_7dae26b6056648ebb404375e","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":t